Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi

I know that in order to set the working directory you need to provide the whole path by setwd("C:/Users/Ayala/Documents"). Is there a more elegant way to do that such that you won't need to provide the whole path (and also switch the \ to /) each time?
I'm doing the Coursera R Programming Course and I need to write a function for which one of the arguments is the directory and as I said I want to set the directory in a more elegant way.
When searching the help I cane across the normalizePath <http://127.0.0.1:31839/library/base/help/normalizePath> and the shortPathName <http://127.0.0.1:31839/library/base/help/shortPathName> but I'm not sure that is the way to go.

I will greatly appreciate a general guidance and not a specific answer because I want to try and figure things on my own.

Best,
Ayala

